(2327360, 321444, 56579, '<td valign="top">the pure white sky looks fake and distracting...my photo has the same problem but since this is advanced editing I did a trick...copy the base layer, then isolate just the sky.  Once you have a layer that is just the sky change it to multiply.  And then just adjust the opacity till you get the desired effect.  As long as there are any clouds in the sky it should bring out something nice.</td>', 'the pure white sky looks fake and distracting...my photo has the same problem but since this is advanced editing I did a trick...copy the base layer, then isolate just the sky.  Once you have a layer that is just the sky change it to multiply.  And then just adjust the opacity till you get the desired effect.  As long as there are any clouds in the sky it should bring out something nice.', '2006-04-19 21:28:25.000000', NULL, 1),
