(2339918, 321485, 16780, '<td valign="top">It feels like there is either not enough or too much of the child in the image.  A single hand or the whole head would look better.  The whisps of hair that are there now are disctracting.</td>', 'It feels like there is either not enough or too much of the child in the image.  A single hand or the whole head would look better.  The whisps of hair that are there now are disctracting.', '2006-04-24 18:40:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339939, 320613, 6999, '<td valign="top">The slightly ironic cleanliness of the ''start'' button is intriguing, and the tonality is likeable; There''s a feeling of lens distortion to the image which comes across to my eye as a stand-ion for any real interest: it''s not a wholly un-photographic thing, actually, but its more about the camera than about the subject, and in that sense represents a modernism in photography that seems rather desperate to me - as though the world seen through the lens were no longer interesting enough in its own right. A technically assured submission, and it prompts thoughts more to the point than most, so I can certainly not score you down for that.</td>', 'The slightly ironic cleanliness of the ''start'' button is intriguing, and the tonality is likeable; There''s a feeling of lens distortion to the image which comes across to my eye as a stand-ion for any real interest: it''s not a wholly un-photographic thing, actually, but its more about the camera than about the subject, and in that sense represents a modernism in photography that seems rather desperate to me - as though the world seen through the lens were no longer interesting enough in its own right. A technically assured submission, and it prompts thoughts more to the point than most, so I can certainly not score you down for that.', '2006-04-24 18:44:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339958, 321724, 6999, '<td valign="top">Quite a harsh light you have chosen, which doesn the tonality of your subject few favours I''m afraid; the composition is not bad, but the image prompts the feeling to me that there may ahve been more to draw out of this structure by showing us the receding cable - perhaps even some sense of whatever it is attached to - more simply, the tension to which your title refers isn''t really so evident in the actual image.</td>', 'Quite a harsh light you have chosen, which doesn the tonality of your subject few favours I''m afraid; the composition is not bad, but the image prompts the feeling to me that there may ahve been more to draw out of this structure by showing us the receding cable - perhaps even some sense of whatever it is attached to - more simply, the tension to which your title refers isn''t really so evident in the actual image.', '2006-04-24 18:47:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339959, 322978, 16780, '<td valign="top">I like the look you were going for, but it seems too processed for my taste.  Old depicts character &amp; the finer details have been smoothed over too much.  I could be wrong, but it also looks like the sky has been burned in a way that makes it very noticable.</td>', 'I like the look you were going for, but it seems too processed for my taste.  Old depicts character & the finer details have been smoothed over too much.  I could be wrong, but it also looks like the sky has been burned in a way that makes it very noticable.', '2006-04-24 18:48:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339969, 321401, 6999, '<td valign="top">TF? TD? My obsession with the dear old things has waned somewhat, though I still keep my own (though not in this league, I''m afraid). It''s an interesting shot, but I think the voiters are going to knock your choice of dual subjects, especially as those balloons aare not so old. Almost a classic example of the kind of fine shot not to submit I would say - obviously you have an ''old'' primary subject, so what''s the problem, huh? Well, the mass of punters don''t see like that ...</td>', 'TF? TD? My obsession with the dear old things has waned somewhat, though I still keep my own (though not in this league, I''m afraid). It''s an interesting shot, but I think the voiters are going to knock your choice of dual subjects, especially as those balloons aare not so old. Almost a classic example of the kind of fine shot not to submit I would say - obviously you have an ''old'' primary subject, so what''s the problem, huh? Well, the mass of punters don''t see like that ...', '2006-04-24 18:51:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339981, 322374, 6999, '<td valign="top">Feels like a squeeze for the chalenge theme I''m afraid, and i think you''ll get hit for it. The voters I''m afraid, take an oh-so-straightforward view. Besides which, the image lacks a sense of impact, a sense of a different and intriguing point of view, and a subtlety of light and composition.</td>', 'Feels like a squeeze for the chalenge theme I''m afraid, and i think you''ll get hit for it. The voters I''m afraid, take an oh-so-straightforward view. Besides which, the image lacks a sense of impact, a sense of a different and intriguing point of view, and a subtlety of light and composition.', '2006-04-24 18:54:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339989, 321430, 16780, '<td valign="top">Beautiful car, but the background is too busy to make the image stand out among almost 400 entries.  If no clear background could be had, you could have tried a quarter panel close up or something similar.</td>', 'Beautiful car, but the background is too busy to make the image stand out among almost 400 entries.  If no clear background could be had, you could have tried a quarter panel close up or something similar.', '2006-04-24 18:57:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339990, 323211, 6999, '<td valign="top">This has an interesting juxtaposition of the organised and the disorganised, in both the progression within the bridge''s boards and the surroundings re the bridge itself; however I think your tonality has strayed so far into the pure black/white world, with few greys, that any sense of photographic representation is almost lost. The composition is slightly at odds with your title too - it''s the tangle of bushes rather than the darkness that seems the reference point of the motion indicated by the bridge.</td>', 'This has an interesting juxtaposition of the organised and the disorganised, in both the progression within the bridge''s boards and the surroundings re the bridge itself; however I think your tonality has strayed so far into the pure black/white world, with few greys, that any sense of photographic representation is almost lost. The composition is slightly at odds with your title too - it''s the tangle of bushes rather than the darkness that seems the reference point of the motion indicated by the bridge.', '2006-04-24 18:57:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2339998, 321701, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very flat light has robbed this of a possible sense of magic, of real age i think. The composition is quite clumsy too - the blue tower/minaret is the obvious draw in this image, and your placement of it in frame doesn''t do anything to aid the movement of the eye through the frame; a corner, a thirds line, at a point of joining of the various lines implied by the roofs ... but here the window and the distance have an equal draw and make the whole rather difficult to enjoy.</td>', 'Very flat light has robbed this of a possible sense of magic, of real age i think. The composition is quite clumsy too - the blue tower/minaret is the obvious draw in this image, and your placement of it in frame doesn''t do anything to aid the movement of the eye through the frame; a corner, a thirds line, at a point of joining of the various lines implied by the roofs ... but here the window and the distance have an equal draw and make the whole rather difficult to enjoy.', '2006-04-24 19:00:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2340002, 321008, 6999, '<td valign="top">Technically accomplished prtrait of a vehicle - as an illustration it''s faultless. In this challenge however ... well, it neither is nor looks that old, and there is little more to the image than its subject - no magic in light, environment, relationships, and no surprise.</td>', 'Technically accomplished prtrait of a vehicle - as an illustration it''s faultless. In this challenge however ... well, it neither is nor looks that old, and there is little more to the image than its subject - no magic in light, environment, relationships, and no surprise.', '2006-04-24 19:02:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2340008, 321680, 6999, '<td valign="top">Well done - you have at least found a sense of the bizarre in this subject; ther''s almost an animal grimace in that radiator venting - and the tonality aids that very well. Perhaps slightly too tightly cropped for really comfortable viewing - always beware the edges of frame if you haven''t the motion, the relationships to pull the eye back in.</td>', 'Well done - you have at least found a sense of the bizarre in this subject; ther''s almost an animal grimace in that radiator venting - and the tonality aids that very well. Perhaps slightly too tightly cropped for really comfortable viewing - always beware the edges of frame if you haven''t the motion, the relationships to pull the eye back in.', '2006-04-24 19:05:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2340010, 320541, 16780, '<td valign="top">I think I see reflections...was this taken through a window?  A polorize filter can cut the reflections when taking pics through glass, but sometimes you still can''t get rid of them all.</td>', 'I think I see reflections...was this taken through a window?  A polorize filter can cut the reflections when taking pics through glass, but sometimes you still can''t get rid of them all.', '2006-04-24 19:05:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2340049, 323204, 16780, '<td valign="top">Well I''m sure this got quite a few comments telling you how you shouldn''t take a pic showing the name on ahead stone.  Commenters were quite vocal when I entered a pic of my nephew''s ;)<br/>That said...I like the lower angle, but the stone taking up the lower left corner takes away from the impact &amp; the sky looks too bright a blue &amp; not quite real.  I probably would have toned down the color or went sepia or B&amp;W.</td>', 'Well I''m sure this got quite a few comments telling you how you shouldn''t take a pic showing the name on ahead stone.  Commenters were quite vocal when I entered a pic of my nephew''s ;)That said...I like the lower angle, but the stone taking up the lower left corner takes away from the impact & the sky looks too bright a blue & not quite real.  I probably would have toned down the color or went sepia or B&W.', '2006-04-24 19:21:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2340148, 321940, 35804, '<td valign="top">I like the point of view and shallow focus...and he''s far too cute to put in soup.  : }</td>', 'I like the point of view and shallow focus...and he''s far too cute to put in soup.  : }', '2006-04-24 20:10:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2340153, 322861, 35804, '<td valign="top">Great texture and light. What''s interesting too are the somewhat "fancy" curtains in the window...there is a story here and a bit of mystery...very nice.</td>', 'Great texture and light. What''s interesting too are the somewhat "fancy" curtains in the window...there is a story here and a bit of mystery...very nice.', '2006-04-24 20:13:18.000000', NULL, 1),
