(2344597, 322969, 24642, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nice finish for a fine shot! Love the sidelong glance! I wonder how many have noticed this was shot with the 10-22mm lens? Except it isn''t :-( EXIF shows 68mm; want to change the lens in the data field? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Robert for pointing out that the lens info was wrong. I forgot to change from the default lens.</td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: Very nice finish for a fine shot! Love the sidelong glance! I wonder how many have noticed this was shot with the 10-22mm lens? Except it isn''t :-( EXIF shows 68mm; want to change the lens in the data field?   Thanks Robert for pointing out that the lens info was wrong. I forgot to change from the default lens.', '2006-04-26 04:54:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2344612, 321776, 10858, '<td valign="top">Wife and husband hand in hand in the TOP 3, congrats! Loveable lights and mood here!</td>', 'Wife and husband hand in hand in the TOP 3, congrats! Loveable lights and mood here!', '2006-04-26 05:06:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2344618, 322908, 42792, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.  And yes Front Element, it should have read A.D.  That''s what happens when I submit something at the last minute and just 15mins before a late bedtime :).  Didn''t mean to make this sound older than it is - don''t need to.  As for the sky being flat, I didn''t really have a choice with the weather being so bad the day I shot this.  But in the end, I thought it makes for a simple stark background to contrast nicely with the rich architecture of the cathedrale.  Maybe I should have just square cropped it to reduce the sky.  The learning continues ...</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments.  And yes Front Element, it should have read A.D.  That''s what happens when I submit something at the last minute and just 15mins before a late bedtime :).  Didn''t mean to make this sound older than it is - don''t need to.  As for the sky being flat, I didn''t really have a choice with the weather being so bad the day I shot this.  But in the end, I thought it makes for a simple stark background to contrast nicely with the rich architecture of the cathedrale.  Maybe I should have just square cropped it to reduce the sky.  The learning continues ...', '2006-04-26 05:16:44.000000', NULL, 0),
