(2345653, 320669, 37719, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a top 20!  At first look I was bothered by the oof portion on the left forground. As I reviewed them for voting, I realized it actually was an important part of the composition (intentional?)  It sets up an ''emergence'' sort of feel.  The colors and the subtle changes and flow in the shot are excellent!!  From gray sky at top down through the soft pastels of the sky to the water and beach is one of the nicest transitional flows of color and contrast - definitely at the right place at the right time. Well done!!  Very nice capture!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-26 08:48:16.</i></td>', 'Congrats on a top 20!  At first look I was bothered by the oof portion on the left forground. As I reviewed them for voting, I realized it actually was an important part of the composition (intentional?)  It sets up an ''emergence'' sort of feel.  The colors and the subtle changes and flow in the shot are excellent!!  From gray sky at top down through the soft pastels of the sky to the water and beach is one of the nicest transitional flows of color and contrast - definitely at the right place at the right time. Well done!!  Very nice capture!!!', '2006-04-26 09:46:04.000000', '2006-04-26 09:48:16.000000', 0),
