(2346888, 323225, 32997, '<td valign="top">awesome shot...glad you didn''t go the typical route and compose it with more sky...the foreground makes it somehow intimidating..makes me feel like I need to hesitate approaching it..</td>', 'awesome shot...glad you didn''t go the typical route and compose it with more sky...the foreground makes it somehow intimidating..makes me feel like I need to hesitate approaching it..', '2006-04-26 15:21:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2346966, 321211, 43148, '<td valign="top">Well, not to beat a dead horse, but to me, also, does not convey "old"! Even the skull looks to be a Halloween decoration - rather than a real skull. Not saying it IS, just appears so, maybe due to the soft texture of your photo! Hope this helps a little, anyway!<br/> <br/>Jacque</td>', 'Well, not to beat a dead horse, but to me, also, does not convey "old"! Even the skull looks to be a Halloween decoration - rather than a real skull. Not saying it IS, just appears so, maybe due to the soft texture of your photo! Hope this helps a little, anyway! Jacque', '2006-04-26 15:42:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347000, 322685, 44945, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the comments.  I''m working on how to get the size bigger when resizing and staying under the 150kb.  The picture is larger on my screen than it is once loaded on the site. I''ll get it figured out.<br/>The whole car wasn''t in the picture cause I didn''t want the whole car in the picture.  That was the way I thought the picture looked best.  It''s something to re-think next time.  But you see pictures all the time with partials of the car.</td>', 'Thank you for all the comments.  I''m working on how to get the size bigger when resizing and staying under the 150kb.  The picture is larger on my screen than it is once loaded on the site. I''ll get it figured out.The whole car wasn''t in the picture cause I didn''t want the whole car in the picture.  That was the way I thought the picture looked best.  It''s something to re-think next time.  But you see pictures all the time with partials of the car.', '2006-04-26 15:49:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347047, 323215, 40718, '<td valign="top">I can''t see your camera settings, but the first thing I thought was the picture was noisy.  It might actually just be the way the brick is on the facade.<br/> <br/>A few thoughts:<br/>1) The color is very drab.  I usually recommend that we switch to black and white in situations like this.  The color is giving us nothing and is probably dragging us down.<br/>2) The composition is very static.  The building is quite centered and it''s a typical "off axis" presentation of a building.<br/>3) The brick, as mentioned above, either didn''t capture well because of the light, or the processing or something.  It looks very muddled and not contrasty enough.  You need more contrast to the picture.</td>', 'I can''t see your camera settings, but the first thing I thought was the picture was noisy.  It might actually just be the way the brick is on the facade. A few thoughts:1) The color is very drab.  I usually recommend that we switch to black and white in situations like this.  The color is giving us nothing and is probably dragging us down.2) The composition is very static.  The building is quite centered and it''s a typical "off axis" presentation of a building.3) The brick, as mentioned above, either didn''t capture well because of the light, or the processing or something.  It looks very muddled and not contrasty enough.  You need more contrast to the picture.', '2006-04-26 15:58:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347064, 323205, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hehehehehe! I feel so loved ;)</td>', 'Hehehehehe! I feel so loved ;)', '2006-04-26 16:03:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347066, 320886, 57151, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by puzzled:</b></div><hr/><i> Ah! I think I get it ... is it a real woman''s head with her body hidden by the curtain and the part from the scarf down is a mannequin? Interesting and colorful entry, however you did it! She looks like she could just get up and scare the bejesus out of me at any second. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>  No trickery here...the mannequin really looks like that.  Pretty creepy, huh?</td>', 'Originally posted by puzzled: Ah! I think I get it ... is it a real woman''s head with her body hidden by the curtain and the part from the scarf down is a mannequin? Interesting and colorful entry, however you did it! She looks like she could just get up and scare the bejesus out of me at any second.    No trickery here...the mannequin really looks like that.  Pretty creepy, huh?', '2006-04-26 16:03:20.000000', NULL, 0),
