(2347167, 322772, 46870, '<td valign="top">wow whata great shot love it,,,,,<br/></td>', 'wow whata great shot love it,,,,,', '2006-04-26 16:25:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347295, 323034, 48928, '<td valign="top">The picture is not a bad picture at all as what the score seems to reflect.  As previously posted alot of your technical aspects were on track.  Alot of people may not realize the camera is really that old.  The camera''s condition is in great shape so it looks new.  I am slowly learning that you have to be very obvious to voters to get your point across, or just plain WOW them to get good scores.  Many people take only a moment or two to vote and then move on so it is important they get the idea right away and it leaves an impact.  The main thing with this is gonna be many people don''t visually "see" old in this picture.<br/>Hope this if of some help.</td>', 'The picture is not a bad picture at all as what the score seems to reflect.  As previously posted alot of your technical aspects were on track.  Alot of people may not realize the camera is really that old.  The camera''s condition is in great shape so it looks new.  I am slowly learning that you have to be very obvious to voters to get your point across, or just plain WOW them to get good scores.  Many people take only a moment or two to vote and then move on so it is important they get the idea right away and it leaves an impact.  The main thing with this is gonna be many people don''t visually "see" old in this picture.Hope this if of some help.', '2006-04-26 16:55:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347309, 322113, 6999, '<td valign="top">There is nothing wrong with MSG; and it''s certainly a more interesting molecule than it''s given credit for; one would think it was a close relative of DDT from the world''s reaction.<br/> <br/>Didn''t see this amongst the few I commented on, and I''m sorry I missed it. I possibly like the B&amp;W approach of the other shot more, but this one makes more use of those tremendous natural tones. Evidently, in terms of the challenge, you were required to be unrepentantly violent in your post processing in order to score well. Still, thanks for putting it in ;-)</td>', 'There is nothing wrong with MSG; and it''s certainly a more interesting molecule than it''s given credit for; one would think it was a close relative of DDT from the world''s reaction. Didn''t see this amongst the few I commented on, and I''m sorry I missed it. I possibly like the B&W approach of the other shot more, but this one makes more use of those tremendous natural tones. Evidently, in terms of the challenge, you were required to be unrepentantly violent in your post processing in order to score well. Still, thanks for putting it in ;-)', '2006-04-26 16:58:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347342, 323205, 43115, '<td valign="top">Cindi,<br/> <br/>I like to think of myself as a thoughtful and refelctive voter who takes his time to figure out the artist''s intended relation to the challenge before I deduct points for DNMC.<br/> <br/>That said, I never would have gotten this without the other comments, and even your hint in Doc''s thread.<br/> <br/>I get it now, and it is, indeed, great, but I probably would have given you a 5 if I had voted on this one.<br/> <br/>Heh, but now that I do get it... I keep chuckling to myself.  :)<br/> <br/><i>Edit:  Me == retard.  Read the title, stoopid.  Still good work though!</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-26 16:09:21.</i></td>', 'Cindi, I like to think of myself as a thoughtful and refelctive voter who takes his time to figure out the artist''s intended relation to the challenge before I deduct points for DNMC. That said, I never would have gotten this without the other comments, and even your hint in Doc''s thread. I get it now, and it is, indeed, great, but I probably would have given you a 5 if I had voted on this one. Heh, but now that I do get it... I keep chuckling to myself.  :) Edit:  Me == retard.  Read the title, stoopid.  Still good work though!', '2006-04-26 17:07:13.000000', '2006-04-26 17:09:21.000000', 0),
(2347425, 322785, 40718, '<td valign="top">Hmm, a few thoughts here.<br/>1) I love the man.  That beard is a wicked subject.<br/>2) The guy is nicely offcentered.<br/>3) I go back and forth between color and B&amp;W.  Color captures that great sign well, but B&amp;W gives it an older feel to it (and that''s what we were going for).<br/>4) A different crop may have helped with more of the donkey displayed.  Unfortunately right now all we get is a portion of the ass''s ass.<br/>5) It''s not like you could have asked him to take it off, but I really think his jacket limits the shot.  It is the most modern looking thing in the shot and that shade green (like fir trees) just never transmits well on a picture.  It dominates too many pixels to be ignored.  Some dodging of this right side to bring it out of the shadows may have helped a bit too.<br/> <br/>I think I would have given this a 5 or 6.</td>', 'Hmm, a few thoughts here.1) I love the man.  That beard is a wicked subject.2) The guy is nicely offcentered.3) I go back and forth between color and B&W.  Color captures that great sign well, but B&W gives it an older feel to it (and that''s what we were going for).4) A different crop may have helped with more of the donkey displayed.  Unfortunately right now all we get is a portion of the ass''s ass.5) It''s not like you could have asked him to take it off, but I really think his jacket limits the shot.  It is the most modern looking thing in the shot and that shade green (like fir trees) just never transmits well on a picture.  It dominates too many pixels to be ignored.  Some dodging of this right side to bring it out of the shadows may have helped a bit too. I think I would have given this a 5 or 6.', '2006-04-26 17:25:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347432, 321301, 2490, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot, and gave it an 8, even though I''m not a "grunge" look fan.</td>', 'I really like this shot, and gave it an 8, even though I''m not a "grunge" look fan.', '2006-04-26 17:27:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347439, 322820, 49652, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully done - it looks like a painting.</td>', 'Wonderfully done - it looks like a painting.', '2006-04-26 17:28:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347441, 322987, 40718, '<td valign="top">The covered bridge is a nice subject.  The presentation is a bit static.  We not only have a very centered composition, but the light is almost directly overhead and that doesn''t give us much to work with.  It also causes the left side of the bridge to fade into shadow.  Perhaps you could have shot either early in the day or late to give it more contrast and hopefully the light would have cast some more interesting shadows to give texture.  I do like the red and wish we could have presented more of the whole side there.  Finally, shooting early or late may have helped the sky which as it is now, while not blown out, isn''t too exciting.</td>', 'The covered bridge is a nice subject.  The presentation is a bit static.  We not only have a very centered composition, but the light is almost directly overhead and that doesn''t give us much to work with.  It also causes the left side of the bridge to fade into shadow.  Perhaps you could have shot either early in the day or late to give it more contrast and hopefully the light would have cast some more interesting shadows to give texture.  I do like the red and wish we could have presented more of the whole side there.  Finally, shooting early or late may have helped the sky which as it is now, while not blown out, isn''t too exciting.', '2006-04-26 17:28:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347464, 323034, 40718, '<td valign="top">Ya, you were robbed.  I''m not saying this is Top 10, but 4.5? Get real.  The technicals are excellent.  It is off center, well lit, sharply focused, etc.  Other 4.5 shots only dream of such good technicals.  I would have given this a 6 or a 7.  It is not 8-10 material because it lacks oomph.  We see a nicely done product shot, but the picture fails to engage us with anything else.  We see the camera in our minds eye, turn it over for a second, and then move on.  I will agree with some of the other people who commented in the thread that this looks too "new".  Sure it''s old, but I think the voter wanted to see scratched and broken.  I was even worried in my shot that the tractor looked too new and think I only got away with it because of the moody sky which lent an "old" feel to the picture.</td>', 'Ya, you were robbed.  I''m not saying this is Top 10, but 4.5? Get real.  The technicals are excellent.  It is off center, well lit, sharply focused, etc.  Other 4.5 shots only dream of such good technicals.  I would have given this a 6 or a 7.  It is not 8-10 material because it lacks oomph.  We see a nicely done product shot, but the picture fails to engage us with anything else.  We see the camera in our minds eye, turn it over for a second, and then move on.  I will agree with some of the other people who commented in the thread that this looks too "new".  Sure it''s old, but I think the voter wanted to see scratched and broken.  I was even worried in my shot that the tractor looked too new and think I only got away with it because of the moody sky which lent an "old" feel to the picture.', '2006-04-26 17:35:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347482, 323205, 40718, '<td valign="top">Well, a nicely done shot Cindi.  You have been around long enough to know that voters don''t do well with abstract.  "old idea" certainly is abstract, especially when it was "new" a month ago and won a ribbon.  I guess we check our sense of humor at the door on this site.  Technicals are done very well and the fractal pattern is quite crazy.  it lacks the color oomph of rikki''s, but that would have made it seem even less old.<br/> <br/>I''ve started calling the narrow minded on the site "knuckleheads".  It somehow makes me feel better.  On this picture, the knuckleheads beat you down.</td>', 'Well, a nicely done shot Cindi.  You have been around long enough to know that voters don''t do well with abstract.  "old idea" certainly is abstract, especially when it was "new" a month ago and won a ribbon.  I guess we check our sense of humor at the door on this site.  Technicals are done very well and the fractal pattern is quite crazy.  it lacks the color oomph of rikki''s, but that would have made it seem even less old. I''ve started calling the narrow minded on the site "knuckleheads".  It somehow makes me feel better.  On this picture, the knuckleheads beat you down.', '2006-04-26 17:39:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347485, 320606, 41008, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.</td>', 'Beautiful.', '2006-04-26 17:40:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347498, 321701, 40718, '<td valign="top">I''m torn on this one.  The blue roof is really cool, but the rest of the picture is blah for color.  When that occurs, I recommend B&amp;W and go with textures and shapes.  I pulled this into PS and tried a B&amp;W treatment.  The blue channel gave it some nice moodiness and then I really upped the contrast and lowered the brightness (+30/-30).  It, to me, gives it more of an actual old feel.  However, then I don''t get to see that cool blue roof, so I don''t know.  The other criticism is the roof is very centered.  Cropping or composition should have thrown that subject to one side or the other.<br/>The technicals are well done except you shot at midday and that always leads to a less interesting picture.  The same at sunrise or sunset would likely have been better.</td>', 'I''m torn on this one.  The blue roof is really cool, but the rest of the picture is blah for color.  When that occurs, I recommend B&W and go with textures and shapes.  I pulled this into PS and tried a B&W treatment.  The blue channel gave it some nice moodiness and then I really upped the contrast and lowered the brightness (+30/-30).  It, to me, gives it more of an actual old feel.  However, then I don''t get to see that cool blue roof, so I don''t know.  The other criticism is the roof is very centered.  Cropping or composition should have thrown that subject to one side or the other.The technicals are well done except you shot at midday and that always leads to a less interesting picture.  The same at sunrise or sunset would likely have been better.', '2006-04-26 17:44:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347530, 321008, 55480, '<td valign="top">Sorry that people were to stupid to believe it was actually old, or just had a dumb stereotype in their head about old things. I wasn''t happy with mine either but when I saw yours I felt bad cuz yours is better than mine.</td>', 'Sorry that people were to stupid to believe it was actually old, or just had a dumb stereotype in their head about old things. I wasn''t happy with mine either but when I saw yours I felt bad cuz yours is better than mine.', '2006-04-26 17:54:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347557, 320690, 42792, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comment but I assure you I still have some to catch up with your average score and number of challenges entered :).  As for this entry, hope you won''t take it badly but you''ve done much much much better stuff than this (you know what I think of some of your work).  Gave this a 5 ''coz there was nothing really out of whack but neither was there anything that grabbed me.  It meets the challenge despite your concern about the shine.  Just wished there was something more to stop me in my tracks.  It "looks" like you just snapped without thinking.  I guess, the question is what did you want to say through this shot?  Ok, it''s old but ... what else..   Not sure the composition or the angle works either.  <br/> <br/>Hope that helps - if not, just dump my feedback ;-).</td>', 'Thanks for the comment but I assure you I still have some to catch up with your average score and number of challenges entered :).  As for this entry, hope you won''t take it badly but you''ve done much much much better stuff than this (you know what I think of some of your work).  Gave this a 5 ''coz there was nothing really out of whack but neither was there anything that grabbed me.  It meets the challenge despite your concern about the shine.  Just wished there was something more to stop me in my tracks.  It "looks" like you just snapped without thinking.  I guess, the question is what did you want to say through this shot?  Ok, it''s old but ... what else..   Not sure the composition or the angle works either.   Hope that helps - if not, just dump my feedback ;-).', '2006-04-26 18:04:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347598, 321776, 33560, '<td valign="top">Congrats. I love the emtyness and the palpable light. It  evokes both a distant  place and  time,  and it presents an oldness  prototypical and mythic.  Super.</td>', 'Congrats. I love the emtyness and the palpable light. It  evokes both a distant  place and  time,  and it presents an oldness  prototypical and mythic.  Super.', '2006-04-26 18:17:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347659, 322588, 42792, '<td valign="top">I think this is a nice product shot and showing the year at the bottom was a nice touch.  Some issues with the white and green reflection on the bottle neck which can be cloned out in PS and I would have preferred a little more detail in the dark areas.  But I like the overall soft effect you chose.  I gave it a 6.</td>', 'I think this is a nice product shot and showing the year at the bottom was a nice touch.  Some issues with the white and green reflection on the bottle neck which can be cloned out in PS and I would have preferred a little more detail in the dark areas.  But I like the overall soft effect you chose.  I gave it a 6.', '2006-04-26 18:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347674, 323034, 29797, '<td valign="top">This shot does NOT deserve this placing. 4.5''s are reserved for photos with not much technical and/or creative merit. This has both of those and then some. It''s a superb shot of the camera! The focus and detail are spot on, as well as the creative lighting you used which gives some nice white reflections on the grip part and the side showing the texture. I too really wonder why the low score. There were a lot of entries in this challenge, and with that number I think some people move a little faster and are looking for the "eye candy" shots. I personally gave it a 6, and probably would''ve bumped it to a 7 had I gone back and looked at the entries a second time like I normally do. I see the "old" to it, I have an old Canon Elan which is almost the same camera. It''s a great shot, and I''m sorry to see the final placement. You do really good work, don''t let this score get you down.</td>', 'This shot does NOT deserve this placing. 4.5''s are reserved for photos with not much technical and/or creative merit. This has both of those and then some. It''s a superb shot of the camera! The focus and detail are spot on, as well as the creative lighting you used which gives some nice white reflections on the grip part and the side showing the texture. I too really wonder why the low score. There were a lot of entries in this challenge, and with that number I think some people move a little faster and are looking for the "eye candy" shots. I personally gave it a 6, and probably would''ve bumped it to a 7 had I gone back and looked at the entries a second time like I normally do. I see the "old" to it, I have an old Canon Elan which is almost the same camera. It''s a great shot, and I''m sorry to see the final placement. You do really good work, don''t let this score get you down.', '2006-04-26 18:48:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347682, 321407, 40718, '<td valign="top">Hmm, I think you got a bit underrated here.  Your technicals are well done.  I especially like the well demarcated shadow against the mausoleum.  Perhaps people didn''t know this was a graveyard (I thought it was a museum at first look).  Not that that should matter.  One thing I don''t quite like is the quadtone.  It looks purple to me and I''m not sure what purple adds to the picture.<br/> <br/>It also lacks just a bit of that "wow" factor.  That''s can be judged by the # of 8-10 votes.  Still, I would have easily given this a 6 if not a 7.  5.3 is low in my opinion.</td>', 'Hmm, I think you got a bit underrated here.  Your technicals are well done.  I especially like the well demarcated shadow against the mausoleum.  Perhaps people didn''t know this was a graveyard (I thought it was a museum at first look).  Not that that should matter.  One thing I don''t quite like is the quadtone.  It looks purple to me and I''m not sure what purple adds to the picture. It also lacks just a bit of that "wow" factor.  That''s can be judged by the # of 8-10 votes.  Still, I would have easily given this a 6 if not a 7.  5.3 is low in my opinion.', '2006-04-26 18:52:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347697, 320865, 40718, '<td valign="top">A few things, although I like the picture and idea overall.<br/>1) The composition is so centered. Boring. You know better than that.<br/>2) The building is awesome, but is just a bit dark.  We lose the great detail of all the wood planks.<br/>3) I think you did a good job on the sky, but to be honest, the tone in the middle is my least favorite color of sky.  It looks like faded slides to me.  That''s just a nitpick though.  I think you did well with the sky.<br/> <br/>It''s mainly the centered composition which got you here, I think.</td>', 'A few things, although I like the picture and idea overall.1) The composition is so centered. Boring. You know better than that.2) The building is awesome, but is just a bit dark.  We lose the great detail of all the wood planks.3) I think you did a good job on the sky, but to be honest, the tone in the middle is my least favorite color of sky.  It looks like faded slides to me.  That''s just a nitpick though.  I think you did well with the sky. It''s mainly the centered composition which got you here, I think.', '2006-04-26 18:58:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347723, 320606, 41746, '<td valign="top">Very mystique image, cold, dark and spooky. Well done, Gísli, congrats on your top ten finish.</td>', 'Very mystique image, cold, dark and spooky. Well done, Gísli, congrats on your top ten finish.', '2006-04-26 19:06:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347740, 320858, 37719, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately I didn''t get to vote on all entries in this challenge.  This is a great shot.  Full of contrasts and opposing feels.  Age - or oldness - seems apparent.  What really strikes me is the difference between the top and bottom half of the shot.  The top seems so smooth and graceful in a way.  The bottom is rough, rigid.  Very nicely composed and the tight crop really helps him/her to stand out for the full frame and not just part of it.  Nice job!  Great image!</td>', 'Unfortunately I didn''t get to vote on all entries in this challenge.  This is a great shot.  Full of contrasts and opposing feels.  Age - or oldness - seems apparent.  What really strikes me is the difference between the top and bottom half of the shot.  The top seems so smooth and graceful in a way.  The bottom is rough, rigid.  Very nicely composed and the tight crop really helps him/her to stand out for the full frame and not just part of it.  Nice job!  Great image!', '2006-04-26 19:10:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2347811, 322820, 10818, '<td valign="top">That is such a fabulous photo.  I just love it.<br/> <br/>Much better then that second place guy.  :)<br/> <br/>Congrats !</td>', 'That is such a fabulous photo.  I just love it. Much better then that second place guy.  :) Congrats !', '2006-04-26 19:29:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348013, 322820, 43901, '<td valign="top">Greaat shot!  I''d love to know your ps treatments.  Congratulations!</td>', 'Greaat shot!  I''d love to know your ps treatments.  Congratulations!', '2006-04-26 20:36:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348023, 323076, 40718, '<td valign="top">The good:<br/>1) The composition uses the rule of thirds nicely.<br/>2) The lighting does create texture and interesting shadow<br/> <br/>To be worked on:<br/>1) The subject doesn''t capture us at all.  We look at it a second and then move on.  You don''t even have to add a new subject, but just more interest.  An example would be the same shot, but you were lucky and had a creeping ivy vine crawling up the wall.  It would give us more to digest.<br/>2) While the lighting does create texture, it''s a bit dark as well.  More light and then more contrast would be beneficial.</td>', 'The good:1) The composition uses the rule of thirds nicely.2) The lighting does create texture and interesting shadow To be worked on:1) The subject doesn''t capture us at all.  We look at it a second and then move on.  You don''t even have to add a new subject, but just more interest.  An example would be the same shot, but you were lucky and had a creeping ivy vine crawling up the wall.  It would give us more to digest.2) While the lighting does create texture, it''s a bit dark as well.  More light and then more contrast would be beneficial.', '2006-04-26 20:40:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348039, 323100, 41337, '<td valign="top">Very underrated photo! Not sure why this got all the low votes.</td>', 'Very underrated photo! Not sure why this got all the low votes.', '2006-04-26 20:45:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348041, 321020, 40667, '<td valign="top">4th!!! Amazing shot really! has to be one of my absolute favs by you, I reaelly wish i had had the time to even glance through the challenge, because i would have commented atleast! Great job Anna!! You Really deserved blue on this challenge!!</td>', '4th!!! Amazing shot really! has to be one of my absolute favs by you, I reaelly wish i had had the time to even glance through the challenge, because i would have commented atleast! Great job Anna!! You Really deserved blue on this challenge!!', '2006-04-26 20:46:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348045, 321445, 40718, '<td valign="top">Last minute entries can be dangerous, eh?<br/> <br/>Actually I think there is some promise to the picture overall. But, yes, it does need some work.<br/> <br/>1) It''s soft.  I didn''t see which lens you were using, but we needed to either a) put it on a tripod if you were handholding at 1/60 or b) increase DOF (which would probably mean you needed a tripod anyway).  You can see the gear in the front is sharper than the gear in back.  Either way, they are both soft.<br/>2) The interesting parts, the gears, are dark while the more boring part (the front) is light.  Could we have moved or manipulated the object or the lighting to reverse this?<br/>3) I would have cropped even tighter to remove the object on the right.  Although some might complain, I may even cut off a small part of the big gear.  That may lead to a my dynamic picture.<br/>4) Many times in pictures that lack strong colors, changing to B&amp;W is helpful.  The picture then becomes one of texture, shape and pattern.  You probably need to increase contrast too, although as is the front will blow out even more so you''d have to fix the lighting first.</td>', 'Last minute entries can be dangerous, eh? Actually I think there is some promise to the picture overall. But, yes, it does need some work. 1) It''s soft.  I didn''t see which lens you were using, but we needed to either a) put it on a tripod if you were handholding at 1/60 or b) increase DOF (which would probably mean you needed a tripod anyway).  You can see the gear in the front is sharper than the gear in back.  Either way, they are both soft.2) The interesting parts, the gears, are dark while the more boring part (the front) is light.  Could we have moved or manipulated the object or the lighting to reverse this?3) I would have cropped even tighter to remove the object on the right.  Although some might complain, I may even cut off a small part of the big gear.  That may lead to a my dynamic picture.4) Many times in pictures that lack strong colors, changing to B&W is helpful.  The picture then becomes one of texture, shape and pattern.  You probably need to increase contrast too, although as is the front will blow out even more so you''d have to fix the lighting first.', '2006-04-26 20:48:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348140, 323219, 2333, '<td valign="top">Dayum, Marc, thought this was ribbon material fur sure! It was my top vote for the challenge. Great work.</td>', 'Dayum, Marc, thought this was ribbon material fur sure! It was my top vote for the challenge. Great work.', '2006-04-26 21:16:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348193, 321008, 3724, '<td valign="top">1947...  same age as me.</td>', '1947...  same age as me.', '2006-04-26 21:31:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348209, 321301, 46468, '<td valign="top">Another nicely done photo, Tim. The bench looks really old but didn''t realize the teddy was so old. The green below the bench really adds to the "old" look of the bench. I like the composition, many people would have included the whole bench, but in my opinion this works much better. Well done</td>', 'Another nicely done photo, Tim. The bench looks really old but didn''t realize the teddy was so old. The green below the bench really adds to the "old" look of the bench. I like the composition, many people would have included the whole bench, but in my opinion this works much better. Well done', '2006-04-26 21:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348309, 322583, 30982, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, Carl!  While the color version is good, I do prefer the way you did this up with the sepia.  I espcially like the bird - adds a bit of life to a very old piece of history.  Well done!</td>', 'Nice shot, Carl!  While the color version is good, I do prefer the way you did this up with the sepia.  I espcially like the bird - adds a bit of life to a very old piece of history.  Well done!', '2006-04-26 21:54:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2348574, 321005, 34938, '<td valign="top">You were robeed on this...I gave it a 9...I cannot believe the 128th place. I really thought you''d be in the top 5</td>', 'You were robeed on this...I gave it a 9...I cannot believe the 128th place. I really thought you''d be in the top 5', '2006-04-26 22:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
