(2352904, 322820, 92, '<td valign="top">Congrats Nasti !!! Woooooooooooooo hoooooooooooo you and Kiwi took top honors !!! Very moody beautiful photo. You have an amazing talent.</td>', 'Congrats Nasti !!! Woooooooooooooo hoooooooooooo you and Kiwi took top honors !!! Very moody beautiful photo. You have an amazing talent.', '2006-04-28 09:47:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2352910, 321776, 92, '<td valign="top">Congrats Kiwi my friend ! You and Nasti ruled this challenge. No big surprise there :) I love the composition/angle of this. The lighting is just beautiful. It looks like early daybreak when grandmom would be making her biscuits and the smell would fill the house and wake you from your sleep. Superb !</td>', 'Congrats Kiwi my friend ! You and Nasti ruled this challenge. No big surprise there :) I love the composition/angle of this. The lighting is just beautiful. It looks like early daybreak when grandmom would be making her biscuits and the smell would fill the house and wake you from your sleep. Superb !', '2006-04-28 09:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2352955, 322913, 18728, '<td valign="top">A BIG WOW !!! Tons of congrats on your well deserving ribbon. This is the first, but I believe its only the start :) I can only wish to capture such details in a low key dramatic photograph such as this. Amazing!</td>', 'A BIG WOW !!! Tons of congrats on your well deserving ribbon. This is the first, but I believe its only the start :) I can only wish to capture such details in a low key dramatic photograph such as this. Amazing!', '2006-04-28 10:11:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2352978, 321020, 36065, '<td valign="top">Anna, this was one of the best shots in the challenge, in my little opinion.  I feel the placing on the site next door was more fitting,  The tonal range you have captured here is close to perfect.  The exposure is super crisp and the composition is very well-done!  I''ve looked this one over many times, and I can''t find anything to correct.  Very nice work!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-28 09:19:38.</i></td>', 'Anna, this was one of the best shots in the challenge, in my little opinion.  I feel the placing on the site next door was more fitting,  The tonal range you have captured here is close to perfect.  The exposure is super crisp and the composition is very well-done!  I''ve looked this one over many times, and I can''t find anything to correct.  Very nice work!', '2006-04-28 10:18:55.000000', '2006-04-28 10:19:38.000000', 0),
(2352988, 323219, 36065, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done.  The wind-blown sand leads the viewer''s eye through the entire shot, sopping by each important element.  The lighting is beautiful, wspecially with the highlight that separates the sand background from the sky.  I''d really like to see the rest of the plant''s shadow.  While you have followed the rule fo thirds to a T, chopping off the shadow leaves me hanging just a little bit.  Overall, and 8 in my little world of voting.</td>', 'Very nicely done.  The wind-blown sand leads the viewer''s eye through the entire shot, sopping by each important element.  The lighting is beautiful, wspecially with the highlight that separates the sand background from the sky.  I''d really like to see the rest of the plant''s shadow.  While you have followed the rule fo thirds to a T, chopping off the shadow leaves me hanging just a little bit.  Overall, and 8 in my little world of voting.', '2006-04-28 10:24:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2353237, 321776, 43432, '<td valign="top">congrats ! beautiful pohoto</td>', 'congrats ! beautiful pohoto', '2006-04-28 12:37:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2353425, 322906, 4411, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pwm6:</b></div><hr/><i>The foreground is soft and the image looks static instead of "in motion."</i></td></tr></table> <br/>The foreground is soft <i>because</i> of the motion :D<br/>It''s very difficult to capture motion in a 3/4 front shot, but check the back wheel.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GoodEnd:</b></div><hr/><i>Bad exposure</i></td></tr></table> <br/>... or bad processing. The exposure is fine, but it''s been run through a Holga action. I think my main mistake was fading a bit of colour back in - it was probably better as a grainy B&amp;W.</td>', 'Originally posted by pwm6:The foreground is soft and the image looks static instead of "in motion." The foreground is soft because of the motion :DIt''s very difficult to capture motion in a 3/4 front shot, but check the back wheel. Originally posted by GoodEnd:Bad exposure ... or bad processing. The exposure is fine, but it''s been run through a Holga action. I think my main mistake was fading a bit of colour back in - it was probably better as a grainy B&W.', '2006-04-28 13:55:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2353434, 321236, 40718, '<td valign="top">Nicely scored with a very simple picture.  11th is a hard place to finish.  I bet you could have hit Top 10 with some sweet radial blur... ;)</td>', 'Nicely scored with a very simple picture.  11th is a hard place to finish.  I bet you could have hit Top 10 with some sweet radial blur... ;)', '2006-04-28 13:58:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2353932, 322091, 37893, '<td valign="top">Congrats on this Shez. The sunset is beautiful as with the shadowed foreground. The DOF control is good in this image and I am glad that it finished as high as it did. Great job.</td>', 'Congrats on this Shez. The sunset is beautiful as with the shadowed foreground. The DOF control is good in this image and I am glad that it finished as high as it did. Great job.', '2006-04-28 17:26:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354395, 320564, 35947, '<td valign="top">You''ve got a nice eye for composition.  Keep at it and submiting to the challenges and you''ll do well!</td>', 'You''ve got a nice eye for composition.  Keep at it and submiting to the challenges and you''ll do well!', '2006-04-28 21:00:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354603, 322214, 37893, '<td valign="top">This image got a 9 from me as well. The textures in this image are great. I can almost smell the old and worn out baseball. Great lighting as well.</td>', 'This image got a 9 from me as well. The textures in this image are great. I can almost smell the old and worn out baseball. Great lighting as well.', '2006-04-28 22:46:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354678, 321301, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very impressed with the editing here!  Also horribly envious of the lush greenery.  Both the bear and the bench do look old to me, and all that lush, new greenery serves as a nice contrast.</td>', 'Very impressed with the editing here!  Also horribly envious of the lush greenery.  Both the bear and the bench do look old to me, and all that lush, new greenery serves as a nice contrast.', '2006-04-28 23:09:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354723, 322035, 30982, '<td valign="top">Now this I rather like!  I suspect the biggest problem as far as score would be it didn''t say "Old" to some.  Compositionally, I like the way you''ve framed the opening, and it''s overall balanced to me.  You''ve done a pretty good job of a hard exposure - getting detail in both the dark and the light sections.  Should you try it again and want to get down and dirty with post processing, I''ve heard taking the shot twice with two different exposures then combining the results can be done.  But I couldn''t tell you how, exactly.  Overall, I find this a solid, appealing picture.</td>', 'Now this I rather like!  I suspect the biggest problem as far as score would be it didn''t say "Old" to some.  Compositionally, I like the way you''ve framed the opening, and it''s overall balanced to me.  You''ve done a pretty good job of a hard exposure - getting detail in both the dark and the light sections.  Should you try it again and want to get down and dirty with post processing, I''ve heard taking the shot twice with two different exposures then combining the results can be done.  But I couldn''t tell you how, exactly.  Overall, I find this a solid, appealing picture.', '2006-04-28 23:18:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354779, 322820, 5792, '<td valign="top">I keep getting drawn back into looking at this landscape again and again. It is a marvelous achievement.</td>', 'I keep getting drawn back into looking at this landscape again and again. It is a marvelous achievement.', '2006-04-28 23:48:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354803, 322035, 36065, '<td valign="top">Pretty cool idea, but I think that the dark area of the capture was overwhelming.  I think if you added a small amount of fill flash inside the barn to bring out just a bit of the old wood detail, you would have scored a bit higher.  It also suffers with the size requirements that we are given.  A larger version would also bring out some of the detail.</td>', 'Pretty cool idea, but I think that the dark area of the capture was overwhelming.  I think if you added a small amount of fill flash inside the barn to bring out just a bit of the old wood detail, you would have scored a bit higher.  It also suffers with the size requirements that we are given.  A larger version would also bring out some of the detail.', '2006-04-29 00:02:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354832, 321301, 36065, '<td valign="top">I really have no idea why this one didn''t finish better.  Perhaps not enough happy color for the DPC masses.  Nice composition and excellent lighting.  Perhaps a closer crop and the elimination of the dead limbs low on the left would have polished it up a bit, but overall a very nice shot.</td>', 'I really have no idea why this one didn''t finish better.  Perhaps not enough happy color for the DPC masses.  Nice composition and excellent lighting.  Perhaps a closer crop and the elimination of the dead limbs low on the left would have polished it up a bit, but overall a very nice shot.', '2006-04-29 00:14:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2354874, 322504, 30982, '<td valign="top">Maybe not "old" as most would perceive it, but works well when taken with the title.  Color is excellent - very rich and vibrant - I like the golden tones to it.  The tree branch on the right does compete for a bit of attention, but not sure how else you could have composed the shot.  DOF is used well here.</td>', 'Maybe not "old" as most would perceive it, but works well when taken with the title.  Color is excellent - very rich and vibrant - I like the golden tones to it.  The tree branch on the right does compete for a bit of attention, but not sure how else you could have composed the shot.  DOF is used well here.', '2006-04-29 00:35:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355258, 321776, 37893, '<td valign="top">Dude! You got whipped by the wifey ;) Great image though. I wish I had somewhere like this that I could shoot ;) COngrats.</td>', 'Dude! You got whipped by the wifey ;) Great image though. I wish I had somewhere like this that I could shoot ;) COngrats.', '2006-04-29 02:49:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355269, 322913, 37893, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on this wonderful entry. This definitely has great tonal qualities to it ;) Great job!</td>', 'Congratulations on this wonderful entry. This definitely has great tonal qualities to it ;) Great job!', '2006-04-29 02:53:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355317, 322504, 53147, '<td valign="top">I am surprised this didnt do better. I found it funny. For me I think the color has an odd yellow/green cast to it all. You may have been able to blend the blur in a bit better on the tree in the immediate background - a bit too much in parts. But still I found it better than a 5.0. Good concept. Maybe going black and white would have been good.</td>', 'I am surprised this didnt do better. I found it funny. For me I think the color has an odd yellow/green cast to it all. You may have been able to blend the blur in a bit better on the tree in the immediate background - a bit too much in parts. But still I found it better than a 5.0. Good concept. Maybe going black and white would have been good.', '2006-04-29 03:01:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355323, 323219, 53147, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot. Great colors and lines and a good neverending fell. I gave you a 7 on this one.</td>', 'Beautiful shot. Great colors and lines and a good neverending fell. I gave you a 7 on this one.', '2006-04-29 03:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355338, 322960, 53147, '<td valign="top">Not a bad shot. Maybe just not enough of the press to give a person a good feel as to what he was looking at. I think you may have fared better had you included more of the press. Good colors and lighting. The sharpness overall is good as well. Just not a picture that draws in your attention.</td>', 'Not a bad shot. Maybe just not enough of the press to give a person a good feel as to what he was looking at. I think you may have fared better had you included more of the press. Good colors and lighting. The sharpness overall is good as well. Just not a picture that draws in your attention.', '2006-04-29 03:05:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355346, 321302, 53147, '<td valign="top">Good shot overall. Personally I think a bit more color would have made it better. Also a wider crop - some more sky and background could help give more of a desolate feel. I scored you higher than your average.</td>', 'Good shot overall. Personally I think a bit more color would have made it better. Also a wider crop - some more sky and background could help give more of a desolate feel. I scored you higher than your average.', '2006-04-29 03:07:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355359, 323190, 53147, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot and perspective. I wonder what a clear day with blue skies would have made this feel. Well done.</td>', 'Very cool shot and perspective. I wonder what a clear day with blue skies would have made this feel. Well done.', '2006-04-29 03:11:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355376, 321758, 53147, '<td valign="top">The wall definitley looks old. But the postprocessing takes away from it unfortunately. The grass seems oversaturated and the trees take away from the detail in the wall. A close up shot of the wall I think would have fared better. Don''t be discouraged - your shots and the votes will improve. (PS - In retrospective I agree with you on my teddy bear shot. You were the first to point it out and it all became clear then. ty)</td>', 'The wall definitley looks old. But the postprocessing takes away from it unfortunately. The grass seems oversaturated and the trees take away from the detail in the wall. A close up shot of the wall I think would have fared better. Don''t be discouraged - your shots and the votes will improve. (PS - In retrospective I agree with you on my teddy bear shot. You were the first to point it out and it all became clear then. ty)', '2006-04-29 03:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2355468, 323219, 37893, '<td valign="top">I pegged this as being in the top ten and I am glad to see you make it ;) Congrats!</td>', 'I pegged this as being in the top ten and I am glad to see you make it ;) Congrats!', '2006-04-29 03:39:35.000000', NULL, 0),
