(2368656, 322504, 2490, '<td valign="top">Somehow I almost missed this one in my Trading Post critiques - sorry.  I gave this shot a 5, and to be honest that was probably a little harsh, second view says "6".  It''s almost monochromatic, in my eye, and there''s a little too much yellow.  The edge of the vertical board that the birdhouse is sitting on has something wierd going on, can''t tell if it''s color related or if it''s something actually in the photo.  <br/> <br/>It SEEMS that a larger aperture to blur the background to obliteration would help this.  I''m continually distracted by all that color back there.  Looks like you''ve done some nice work to get good solid "edges" in the photo, but the background bothers me.<br/> <br/>I do like the overall composition, with the exception of that tree limb poking into the side of the subject.</td>', 'Somehow I almost missed this one in my Trading Post critiques - sorry.  I gave this shot a 5, and to be honest that was probably a little harsh, second view says "6".  It''s almost monochromatic, in my eye, and there''s a little too much yellow.  The edge of the vertical board that the birdhouse is sitting on has something wierd going on, can''t tell if it''s color related or if it''s something actually in the photo.   It SEEMS that a larger aperture to blur the background to obliteration would help this.  I''m continually distracted by all that color back there.  Looks like you''ve done some nice work to get good solid "edges" in the photo, but the background bothers me. I do like the overall composition, with the exception of that tree limb poking into the side of the subject.', '2006-05-01 14:13:42.000000', NULL, 0),
