(2386122, 323046, 51538, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure in what conditions you took the photo, but I think it would be possible to get greater clarity especially considering the IS of the lens and speed of shutter used.  The scene had great potential for an interesting and high quality photo.</td>', 'I''m not sure in what conditions you took the photo, but I think it would be possible to get greater clarity especially considering the IS of the lens and speed of shutter used.  The scene had great potential for an interesting and high quality photo.', '2006-05-05 21:47:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2387163, 323197, 35161, '<td valign="top">Love the warm colors and the textures are great! :)</td>', 'Love the warm colors and the textures are great! :)', '2006-05-06 09:51:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2390103, 320658, 19670, '<td valign="top">I found myself trying to scroll to see the "rest" of the top of the image. The black surround makes it seem like there''s a border. I wonder if you could have gotten an angle from further left to hide the pole and then clone out the power lines? The broken glass is interseting as a foreground element.</td>', 'I found myself trying to scroll to see the "rest" of the top of the image. The black surround makes it seem like there''s a border. I wonder if you could have gotten an angle from further left to hide the pole and then clone out the power lines? The broken glass is interseting as a foreground element.', '2006-05-07 15:10:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2390499, 322142, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Very Nice shot, has the WOW factor.<br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Very good composition. Just wondering if it''s little bit tilted.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>I really like the subject. Definately meets the challenge.<br/>Technical (Colour and light): <br/>Veri nice colors and ligting. If I am not wrong you used Dodging and Burning in PP. Works for me, nice.<br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>The picture needs to rotated little bit. Just wondering if it was possible for you to take this from different angle, may be moving further to the right side.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Very nice image, good PP. Meet the Challenge, has some WOW factor for me.<br/> <br/>Over all very nice image. Congrates on your Personal Best.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. First Impression Very Nice shot, has the WOW factor.Composition: Very good composition. Just wondering if it''s little bit tilted.Subject: I really like the subject. Definately meets the challenge.Technical (Colour and light): Veri nice colors and ligting. If I am not wrong you used Dodging and Burning in PP. Works for me, nice.Improvement: The picture needs to rotated little bit. Just wondering if it was possible for you to take this from different angle, may be moving further to the right side.Summary: Very nice image, good PP. Meet the Challenge, has some WOW factor for me. Over all very nice image. Congrates on your Personal Best.', '2006-05-07 19:01:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2393034, 321428, 56658, '<td valign="top">I think this one may have worked better in color. normally I like B/W to convey some mood but I think the color and marks on the toy surronded by the trash may have worked.</td>', 'I think this one may have worked better in color. normally I like B/W to convey some mood but I think the color and marks on the toy surronded by the trash may have worked.', '2006-05-08 11:40:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394275, 322917, 19919, '<td valign="top">I like the composition, but maybe if you had tried the shot a little earlier/later in the day.  This would have reduced some of the harsh shadows!<br/> <br/>edit:  added both ends of the day!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-08 16:44:55.</i></td>', 'I like the composition, but maybe if you had tried the shot a little earlier/later in the day.  This would have reduced some of the harsh shadows! edit:  added both ends of the day!', '2006-05-08 17:43:54.000000', '2006-05-08 17:44:55.000000', 0),
(2394290, 322917, 55642, '<td valign="top">I think the building behind the truck detracts from the composition, but mostly I think you probably suffered from rusted car overload. DPC sees way too many, especially in challenges where it''s just much too easy to throw one in.</td>', 'I think the building behind the truck detracts from the composition, but mostly I think you probably suffered from rusted car overload. DPC sees way too many, especially in challenges where it''s just much too easy to throw one in.', '2006-05-08 17:48:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394297, 322917, 49716, '<td valign="top">Another thing to try would be to move further back and zoom in.  This would compress the perspective and concentrate the eye on the tones and textures.</td>', 'Another thing to try would be to move further back and zoom in.  This would compress the perspective and concentrate the eye on the tones and textures.', '2006-05-08 17:50:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394339, 322917, 49007, '<td valign="top">In my opinion the image suffers from being oversaturated. Also the composition is bright in the upper right and dark shadows in the lower left. Needs some balance in that regard. Try cropping out from the turnsignal up and mid bumper down (landscape).</td>', 'In my opinion the image suffers from being oversaturated. Also the composition is bright in the upper right and dark shadows in the lower left. Needs some balance in that regard. Try cropping out from the turnsignal up and mid bumper down (landscape).', '2006-05-08 18:00:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394550, 322917, 34192, '<td valign="top">This image has an excellent point of view but I agree with a previous commenter - crop more of the image. Often, in pictures, less is more - let the viewer fill in all the other details - we don''t need the rest of the truck to know what it is.  In this challenge, I gave you a 6 - it was a well taken image.</td>', 'This image has an excellent point of view but I agree with a previous commenter - crop more of the image. Often, in pictures, less is more - let the viewer fill in all the other details - we don''t need the rest of the truck to know what it is.  In this challenge, I gave you a 6 - it was a well taken image.', '2006-05-08 19:06:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395114, 323046, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hello from me via the CTP2 thread!<br/> <br/>The color and model''s expression are very good. However, here''s where things get rough:<br/> <br/>The crop is way too tight. The top of the head is cut off, along with most of the body and cross. Particularly the hands. The cross is an important element in the photo, but it''s been truncated. <br/> <br/>The noise is distracting. I know I tend to add noise when I''m trying to cover up an unsalvageable lack of sharpness, so it makes me wonder why that decision was made unless it''s designed to hide a flaw like that. Otherwise, it seems rather unnecessary.<br/> <br/>Finally, the biggest reason I think that photos failed in this challenge was that they just did not convey a sense of "old". "Old" needed to be projected as a concept, and that''s just not the first thing that pops into my head when I look at this. The model is young. I think of religious pageantry. I don''t automatically think "old". Most Western Christian portrayals of the Stations of the Cross will involve a crown of thorns, which is conspicuously missing from the photo. I don''t think that Senakulo is very familiar to most of the DPC audience, and anything unfamiliar tends to get voted down. <br/> <br/>My only suggestion here, really, is to give more consideration to what the DPC audience is going to want to see. On abstract concepts like "Something Old",  make sure the photo screams "OLD!" as loudly as possible.</td>', 'Hello from me via the CTP2 thread! The color and model''s expression are very good. However, here''s where things get rough: The crop is way too tight. The top of the head is cut off, along with most of the body and cross. Particularly the hands. The cross is an important element in the photo, but it''s been truncated.  The noise is distracting. I know I tend to add noise when I''m trying to cover up an unsalvageable lack of sharpness, so it makes me wonder why that decision was made unless it''s designed to hide a flaw like that. Otherwise, it seems rather unnecessary. Finally, the biggest reason I think that photos failed in this challenge was that they just did not convey a sense of "old". "Old" needed to be projected as a concept, and that''s just not the first thing that pops into my head when I look at this. The model is young. I think of religious pageantry. I don''t automatically think "old". Most Western Christian portrayals of the Stations of the Cross will involve a crown of thorns, which is conspicuously missing from the photo. I don''t think that Senakulo is very familiar to most of the DPC audience, and anything unfamiliar tends to get voted down.  My only suggestion here, really, is to give more consideration to what the DPC audience is going to want to see. On abstract concepts like "Something Old",  make sure the photo screams "OLD!" as loudly as possible.', '2006-05-08 22:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395132, 322473, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hello from your CTP2 thread!<br/> <br/>Irving Penn or no, I think this photo is a little too straightforward to be competitive on DPC. There is such gorgeous detail in the gown that it''s a pity the light is so harsh. I would have liked to see a more diffused light and more use of shadow to really bring out the stitch detail. <br/> <br/>Also, in a concept challenge like "Something Old", it''s never a good sign when you have to tell your audience that the subject is old. The photo should project that concept all on its own. The worn green blanket is a good start, it gives a sort of musty implication, but it just doesn''t go far enough.</td>', 'Hello from your CTP2 thread! Irving Penn or no, I think this photo is a little too straightforward to be competitive on DPC. There is such gorgeous detail in the gown that it''s a pity the light is so harsh. I would have liked to see a more diffused light and more use of shadow to really bring out the stitch detail.  Also, in a concept challenge like "Something Old", it''s never a good sign when you have to tell your audience that the subject is old. The photo should project that concept all on its own. The worn green blanket is a good start, it gives a sort of musty implication, but it just doesn''t go far enough.', '2006-05-08 22:43:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2396435, 323197, 5728, '<td valign="top">wonderful image Sher, could you tell us a little about the processing here?</td>', 'wonderful image Sher, could you tell us a little about the processing here?', '2006-05-09 08:32:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2396665, 323046, 42125, '<td valign="top">Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-) <br/>This picture has potential.<br/>What is good?:<br/>1. The subject is good.<br/>2. The model is good, good expression on his face.<br/>3. Cropping is good, leading lines make you look at all the picture.<br/>What could be done better?:<br/>1. Title is not good. I would prefer "Old religion" or something like that.<br/>2. Too much red colour<br/>3. The picture is grainy. It is well possible that you did that on purpose but I think that it would be a lot better without it. Try using NeatImage to take away the grain.<br/>4. To much light on his cheeks.<br/>Overall a good picture that scored IMO to low.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 20:27:41.</i></td>', 'Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-) This picture has potential.What is good?:1. The subject is good.2. The model is good, good expression on his face.3. Cropping is good, leading lines make you look at all the picture.What could be done better?:1. Title is not good. I would prefer "Old religion" or something like that.2. Too much red colour3. The picture is grainy. It is well possible that you did that on purpose but I think that it would be a lot better without it. Try using NeatImage to take away the grain.4. To much light on his cheeks.Overall a good picture that scored IMO to low.', '2006-05-09 10:31:37.000000', '2006-05-10 21:27:41.000000', 0),
(2397547, 323046, 40465, '<td valign="top">Hi from the CTP2 club:)<br/> <br/>I like this image. Its a bit grainy for my liking. The stripes on the shirt in the background are a bit distracting...<br/>Maybe if you left more of the cross in?<br/>The colours are nice, they help with the mood.</td>', 'Hi from the CTP2 club:) I like this image. Its a bit grainy for my liking. The stripes on the shirt in the background are a bit distracting...Maybe if you left more of the cross in?The colours are nice, they help with the mood.', '2006-05-09 16:28:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2398338, 323228, 44490, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments.  I''ve added details to the photographer''s comments above.  For what could have been, please see <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=332273" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Historical and Classical II.</a> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-09 20:17:43.</i></td>', 'Thanks for your comments.  I''ve added details to the photographer''s comments above.  For what could have been, please see Historical and Classical II. ', '2006-05-09 21:12:25.000000', '2006-05-09 21:17:43.000000', 0),
(2398355, 322570, 42506, '<td valign="top">First try or not, I think you did a fantastic job. This is v good shot. I would have guessed this would have gotten a 6 - I guess not quite old enough. Colours / idea / creativity / dof were all great tho. Well done!</td>', 'First try or not, I think you did a fantastic job. This is v good shot. I would have guessed this would have gotten a 6 - I guess not quite old enough. Colours / idea / creativity / dof were all great tho. Well done!', '2006-05-09 21:22:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2398367, 322570, 16912, '<td valign="top">happyitude? now, thats a new word I''m going to start using!<br/> <br/>Congrats on an excellent debut shot! For me a lone ''old'' paintbrush would have bumped this up even more.</td>', 'happyitude? now, thats a new word I''m going to start using! Congrats on an excellent debut shot! For me a lone ''old'' paintbrush would have bumped this up even more.', '2006-05-09 21:27:15.000000', NULL, 0),
