(2497145, 321374, 30982, '<td valign="top">Hmmm - this looks familiar.  :-)  But is it Concepcion or San Jose?  Whichever it is, you captured the subtle colors perfectly!</td>', 'Hmmm - this looks familiar.  :-)  But is it Concepcion or San Jose?  Whichever it is, you captured the subtle colors perfectly!', '2006-06-08 00:10:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2505743, 323201, 48298, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  Love the mist over the sea in the background, as well.  Very nice mood to this.  Great color and fantastic find!</td>', 'Beautiful!  Love the mist over the sea in the background, as well.  Very nice mood to this.  Great color and fantastic find!', '2006-06-10 23:34:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2508946, 323093, 58947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mk:</b></div><hr/><i>The line of the headstone leads your eye into a bit of a dead end though...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry, but that line cracked me up! And it also caused me wonder if that was a part of the photographer''s intent, as, well, it''s Ol'' Dooley''s dead end. :p<br/> <br/>I like it.</td>', 'Originally posted by mk:The line of the headstone leads your eye into a bit of a dead end though...  Sorry, but that line cracked me up! And it also caused me wonder if that was a part of the photographer''s intent, as, well, it''s Ol'' Dooley''s dead end. :p I like it.', '2006-06-12 10:13:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2559891, 322091, 60236, '<td valign="top">Great shot...I love the orange reflection on the sand...a really nice touch</td>', 'Great shot...I love the orange reflection on the sand...a really nice touch', '2006-06-28 00:14:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2563849, 321948, 46314, '<td valign="top">Feels kinda weird commenting on a Langdon photo. Almost like talking to God... Ok, maybe not exactly.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I was perusing, as I am wont to do...<br/>Actually wanted to see how active you still are in the challenges.<br/> <br/>There''s only one improvement I''d like to see on this photo... crop off the bottom part of the driveway - just above those dark patches. That way you retain the drive leading up to the house as Fotomann mentioned, but you also remove those really distracting dark patches.<br/> <br/>I just masked that portion with my hand, and immediately that house leapt out at me much more...</td>', 'Feels kinda weird commenting on a Langdon photo. Almost like talking to God... Ok, maybe not exactly. Anyway, I was perusing, as I am wont to do...Actually wanted to see how active you still are in the challenges. There''s only one improvement I''d like to see on this photo... crop off the bottom part of the driveway - just above those dark patches. That way you retain the drive leading up to the house as Fotomann mentioned, but you also remove those really distracting dark patches. I just masked that portion with my hand, and immediately that house leapt out at me much more...', '2006-06-28 20:34:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2588713, 322567, 52731, '<td valign="top">Interesting subject, good composition, nice colors and focus. I would''ve expected a shot like this to place in the 6''s at least. I think that you were voted down a lot because your photo, while obviously featuring an old subject - trees don''t grow that thick overnight - doesn''t match what their pre-concieved notions about what should be in the challenge are, especially the bright colors. Also, since most voters only glance at a photo for a couple of seconds, the bright colors and live grass would register in their brains and leave more of an impression than taking the time to think that a tree is very old would.</td>', 'Interesting subject, good composition, nice colors and focus. I would''ve expected a shot like this to place in the 6''s at least. I think that you were voted down a lot because your photo, while obviously featuring an old subject - trees don''t grow that thick overnight - doesn''t match what their pre-concieved notions about what should be in the challenge are, especially the bright colors. Also, since most voters only glance at a photo for a couple of seconds, the bright colors and live grass would register in their brains and leave more of an impression than taking the time to think that a tree is very old would.', '2006-07-05 17:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2612116, 321020, 48541, '<td valign="top">This has a great b &amp; w film look for being digital.  I think no one noticed the improper use of the camera in the photo because the photo is beautiful, powerful, awesome.</td>', 'This has a great b & w film look for being digital.  I think no one noticed the improper use of the camera in the photo because the photo is beautiful, powerful, awesome.', '2006-07-11 21:33:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2617277, 323219, 34659, '<td valign="top">WOW!  Outstanding shot.  Absolutely stunning...  New Favorite!  :-)</td>', 'WOW!  Outstanding shot.  Absolutely stunning...  New Favorite!  :-)', '2006-07-13 01:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
